summary_judge.user:
Compare the SUMMARY with the SOURCE and give three scores from 1 (poor) to 5 (no fault):
- consistency: the summary does not contradict the source and does not mix up years, units or directions of change;
- completeness: the main finding and the main supporting facts of the source are present;
- factual_alignment: every number and claim in the summary can be found in the source.
List each fault you find as one short sentence that quotes the summary words at fault.
A score below 5 must be explained by at least one listed fault.
SOURCE ({{ title }}, PDF pages {{ pages }}):
{{ text }}

SUMMARY:
{{ summary }}

